{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.QbetaDeltaTauCanonicalConditionalQ2Minus1Factor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.QbetaDeltaTauCanonicalConditionalQ2Minus1Factor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPerBlockChiClosedForms"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one_via_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one_via_factor","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-delta-tau-canonical-conditional-q2-minus-1-factor.lean#L69-L81","doc":"**Corollary (vanishing at q = 1 from the factorisation).** As an\nimmediate consequence of the factorisation,\n$\\Delta\\tau_M^{\\text{can}}(1) = 0$.\n\nThis is the same vanishing already proved as\n`delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one` in the parent block; we restate\nit here as a corollary of the factorisation to make the structural\nconnection explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_has_q2_minus_1_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_has_q2_minus_1_factor","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-delta-tau-canonical-conditional-q2-minus-1-factor.lean#L46-L67","doc":"**Theorem (conditional on `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3`,\n§3b-cond pattern).** The canonical $\\Delta\\tau_M$ factors $(q^2 - 1)$\nfor any $q > 0$.\n\n**Proof.** By `chi_blocks_have_q2_minus_1_factor` each per-block\n$\\chi_\\lambda(q) = (q^2 - 1) \\cdot P_\\lambda(q)$. Substituting into\n`delta_tau_M_canonical` and factoring out $(q^2 - 1)$ from the\nweighted sum gives the claim with\n$P^{\\text{can}}(q) = y_3(q) P_3(q) + y_{21}(q) P_{21}(q) + y_{111}(q) P_{111}(q)$.\n\nThis is fully verified by Lean modulo the single class instance —\nthe §3b-cond conditional rigour pattern. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qbeta-delta-tau-canonical-conditional-q2-minus-1-factor","label":"prop:qbeta-delta-tau-canonical-conditional-q2-minus-1-factor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-delta-tau-canonical-conditional-q2-minus-1-factor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}